THE FIRST CAPTURE IN THIS REPOSITORY WITH UNITS DRAWN AS MODELS. 201/5-02 and 5/04 have owed it since the budget was written (150 units, each drawn as a model with a symbol over it) and it has never been takeable: every pak the console ever ran was converted with MODELS=0, so `unitsAsModels` read 0 on every capture and the fallback drew symbols. The blocker was never code — the unit-model path resolved names, opened archives over Range requests and logged `this build carries no model of that name` exactly as designed. It was a convert.

READ THIS AS A FIRST LOOK, NOT AS A ROUTE ROW. It is deliberately filed apart from the 09-05 series and may not be subtracted from any of it:

  - the pak is NEW (`07:40 05-09-2026`, built this session into its own OUT so the `19:23 28-08-2026` pak every other 09-05 row was measured on survives);
  - the ten-leg route was NOT flown — the camera drifted under a hand during the window (it ends at h15 pitch -0.53, not the settle pose);
  - 260 moving frames, below the 300 the collector itself asks for before a percentile is cited;
  - three model TYPES, not the five the board asks for since this session's seed change — the app on the device is still the previous build.

WHAT IT IS GOOD FOR is the structural counts, which are pose-independent in the way that matters: how many draws, how many triangles and how much memory 150 units as models actually cost. Those are the numbers 201's budget was written against and nobody had.

THE HEADLINE: 12 197 DRAWS. The empty field run on the same district draws 96. The frame audit written hours earlier predicted the draw count would move 'by an order of magnitude' at this load and ranked its whole gap list as provisional until somebody measured it; the real figure is 127x, and 1.3 M triangles against 242 k. That is not a frame with more objects in it, it is a different renderer's problem — and it moves the audit's GPU-driven-culling entry (its 3.3) from 'interesting only at 3.1's load' to the load itself.

AND THE SECOND NUMBER IS THE SYMBOLOGY, which 5/02 owes separately: `overlay-2d` is 6.17 ms of an 11.65 ms CPU body at 150 units, against 0.5-0.9 ms on the empty map. The 2D layer is now the largest CPU line in the frame by a factor of two over `engine-frame`.

